# What the npm tarball does NOT ship.
#
# The npm package exists for one thing: the `session-sitter` command, so `npx session-sitter` and
# `npm i -g` work for someone who is never going to install a VS Code extension. Everything here is
# either build input, another front end's packaging, or a test.
#
# ## Why this file exists at all, rather than a `files` array
#
# `files` in package.json would be the obvious way to express an allowlist, and it cannot be used:
# **vsce refuses to run when both `.vscodeignore` and `files` are present** ("VSCE does not support
# combining both strategies"), so adding `files` breaks `make package` and the .vsix with it. vsce
# prefers `.vscodeignore` when it exists and never reads `.npmignore`, so the two packagings stay
# independent — which is the property worth having, because they ship different things: the extension
# needs `resources/` and no CLI entry point, the tarball needs the opposite.
#
# ## Why `out/` is not listed here
#
# It is in `.gitignore`, and npm falls back to `.gitignore` **only when there is no `.npmignore`**.
# The existence of this file is therefore what puts the compiled output into the tarball at all; the
# `prepare` script is what makes sure it has been built. Removing this file does not make the package
# bigger — it makes it empty of the one thing it is for.

# ── Build input ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
src/
tsconfig.json
vitest.config.ts
.eslintrc.json
Makefile
scripts/
ci/
.github/

# ── Compiled tests and source maps ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The tests are not the product, and a source map without its `src/` resolves to nothing.
out/test/
*.js.map

# ── The other two front ends ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Claude Code plugin ships as a git ref, and the extension as a .vsix. Neither reaches a user
# through npm, and `plugin/lib/` alone would roughly double the tarball.
plugin/
.claude-plugin/
resources/
*.vsix
.vscodeignore
skills/

# ── Development tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benchmarks and the screenshot harness need a checkout and a browser, neither of which an npm
# install has.
tools/

# ── Docs, except the one this package is about ──────────────────────────────
#
# `docs/*` and not `docs/`: gitignore semantics cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so excluding the directory outright makes the `!` below dead and — as observed — leaves
# every screenshot in the tarball. 14 MB of PNGs for a command-line tool.
docs/*
!docs/CLI.md
knowledge/

# ── Local and editor state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.vscode/
.vscode-test/
CLAUDE.md
